  "name": "Sleeping Box",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Price</strong> 10 gp; <strong>Weight</strong> 4 lbs.</p>\n<p>This well-constructed box is almost appropriately sized for a single Medium-sized creature to sit or curl up inside of. Some of these boxes are decorated or padded with small pillows and soft fabrics. Depending on its construction, the sleeping box can be folded up or broken down to be reconstructed at a later date for easier storage and transport, but nicer sleeping boxes are not able to be deconstructed in this manner. Sleeping boxes are very popular amongst catfolk, especially smaller breeds of catfolk like the small-paws, but have begun to gain popularity amongst some more eclectic communities of kitsune and other beastfolk.</p>\n<p>Whenever a creature sleeps for at least 2 hours in a sleeping box, they awaken refreshed, gaining 1d4 temporary hit points which last until removed. If a creature would have temporary hit points from multiple sources, these temporary hit points are always lost first.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/adventuring-gear#toc18\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
